  "narrative": "No new validation evidence was released in this final synthesis, and no claim has an open validation response deadline; the voluntary validation budget is exhausted, so the synthesis uses the accumulated discovery evidence plus previously released validation. The strongest supported dataset-internal associations are SMARCA4 loss, KEAP1 loss, TP53 loss, and MSI-high. For direction claims, the estimates are already signed to the claimed hypothesis, and the endpoint is a composite dependency score in which more negative values mean stronger dependency. SMARCA4 loss is robustly associated with stronger dependency: discovery +0.832 with lower bound +0.767 (R9), validated +0.803 with lower bound +0.699 (R26). KEAP1 loss is robustly associated with weaker dependency: discovery +0.832 with lower bound +0.766 (R11), validated +0.803 with lower bound +0.702 (R125). TP53 loss is robustly associated with weaker dependency, though smaller: discovery +0.423 with lower bound +0.327 (R7), validated +0.346 with lower bound +0.217 (R39). MSI-high is robustly associated with stronger dependency: discovery +0.792 with lower bound +0.676 (R52), validated +0.826 with lower bound +0.635 (R66). These effects are large relative to the 0.15 composite-unit threshold, direction-consistent, and robust across multiple technical and biological contexts, so they are reportable as dataset-internal associations but not as causal single-gene essentiality, clinical, or generalizable claims. PTEN loss should be reported as context-dependent, not as a global predictor. Broad or adult global PTEN-loss contrasts with positive point estimates above threshold still have lower confidence bounds below threshold, including the direction- -1 PTEN contrasts represented by R38 +0.227 with lower bound +0.131, validated R53 +0.290 with lower bound +0.143, and adult broad PTEN R234 +0.255 with lower bound +0.145. By contrast, controlled contexts are threshold-clear: adult TP53-intact MSI-nonhigh PTEN-loss R243 +0.294 with lower bound +0.188; QC-complete adult TP53/KEAP1-intact MSI-nonhigh PTEN-loss R245 +0.329 with lower bound +0.212; and several earlier genomically constrained adult contexts such as R79 and R164. The elevated-MYC TP53-intact MSI-nonhigh PTEN-loss test remains boundary/underpowered, R244 +0.275 with lower bound +0.128, and should not be promoted to a MYC-specific predictor. Negative findings are extensive. The constructed marker and signature panel is null or far below threshold (R1 through R6). Many measured genomic alterations lack meaningful associations: KRAS R12, STK11 R24, MTAP R25, ARID1A R10, RB1 R76, NF1 R77, SMAD4 R78, MYC amplification R65, EGFR amplification R104, BRAF R105, ERBB2 R49, PIK3CA R50, BRCA2 R51, and APC R72. CDKN2A was not retained as meaningful because estimates cluster below threshold or are imprecise across main, validation, and stratified analyses (R8, R13, R37, R64, R153, R154, R174, R241). Technical or covariate main effects are not meaningful predictors: media serum R91, sex R92, matched omics R36, and CRISPR-library main effect R35 are small or below threshold. Most subgroup-interaction searches are null or imprecise; the accepted central effects do not depend on a clear effect-modifying interaction. Remaining uncertainty is concentrated in PTEN context boundaries, some smaller library or screen-quality strata such as Ky-library TP53 tests (R201, R209, R238), and borderline interactions including KEAP1-adherent culture R229 lower bound +0.018, MSI-adherent culture R240 lower bound +0.110, KEAP1-screen NNMD R221 lower bound +0.022, and PTEN-screen NNMD R242 lower bound -0.028. The most informative next analysis is not further exploratory mining but a prespecified replication of the four central associations in an orthogonal dependency assay or cohort, stratified by lineage, ploidy/aneuploidy, mutation burden, MSI status, screen quality/Cas9 activity, QC completeness, and library context. For PTEN specifically, the only context worth prespecifying is adult TP53-intact MSI-nonhigh, rather than global or MYC-specific claims. No further comparisons are proposed in this run because the central associations are already validated and continued searching would mainly increase multiplicity risk without substantially improving scientific resolution.",
  "research_notes": "FINAL SYNTHESIS (run 23/25). No new validation was released; validation budget exhausted.\\n\\nCentral supported associations (signed estimates; outcome is composite dependency, more negative = stronger dependency; threshold 0.15):\\n- SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency: R9 +0.832 lower 0.767; validated R26 +0.803 lower 0.699.\\n- KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency: R11 +0.832 lower 0.766; validated R125 +0.803 lower 0.702.\\n- TP53 loss -> weaker dependency: R7 +0.423 lower 0.327; validated R39 +0.346 lower 0.217.\\n- MSI-high -> stronger dependency: R52 +0.792 lower 0.676; validated R66 +0.826 lower 0.635.\\nAll four are large, threshold-clear, direction-consistent, and robust across multiple contexts. They are observational dataset-internal associations, not causal or essentiality claims.\\n\\nPTEN-loss is context-dependent, not global. Broad/adult contrasts can have positive point estimates but lower bounds below threshold: direction- -1 PTEN tests represented by R38 +0.227 lower 0.131, validated R53 +0.290 lower 0.143, adult broad R234 +0.255 lower 0.145. Controlled threshold-clear contexts include: adult TP53-intact MSI-nonhigh PTEN-loss R243 +0.294 lower 0.188; QC-complete adult TP53/KEAP1-intact MSI-nonhigh PTEN-loss R245 +0.329 lower 0.212; constrained contexts such as R79 and R164. Elevated-MYC TP53-intact MSI-nonhigh PTEN-loss R244 +0.275 lower 0.128 remains unresolved; do not claim MYC specificity.\\n\\nNegative/null findings: constructed markers/signatures R1-R6; KRAS R12; STK11 R24; MTAP R25; ARID1A R10; RB1 R76; NF1 R77; SMAD4 R78; MYC amplification R65; EGFR amplification R104; BRAF R105; ERBB2 R49; PIK3CA R50; BRCA2 R51; APC R72. CDKN2A not meaningful after audit: R8, R13, R37, R64, R153, R154, R174, R241. Technical/covariate main effects not meaningful: media serum R91, sex R92, matched omics R36, CRISPR-library main effect R35. Most interactions are null or imprecise.\\n\\nUnresolved uncertainty: PTEN context boundaries; Ky-library TP53 strata R201, R209, R238; borderline interactions KEAP1-adherent R229 lower 0.018, MSI-adherent R240 lower 0.110, KEAP1-screen NNMD R221 lower 0.022, PTEN-screen NNMD R242 lower -0.028; some no-evidence registered interactions.\\n\\nFinal recommendation: no further exploratory within-run mining. Prespecify orthogonal replication of SMARCA4, KEAP1, TP53, and MSI-high with stratification by lineage, ploidy/aneuploidy, mutation burden, MSI, screen quality/Cas9, QC completeness, and library context. For PTEN, replicate only the adult TP53-intact MSI-nonhigh context unless prespecified. All conclusions are limited to the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, clinical transportability, or generalizability."
